Drop the newline that ends the last record in awk's paragraph mode.
With RS set to "", a record ends at a run of two or more newlines, but
at the end of the input the last record also ends at a single newline.
It kept that newline instead, so $0 had a trailing newline, and with a
single-character FS other than space, which newline also separates, NF
counted an extra empty field. Leave the newline out of the record and
put it in RT.

---
 editors/awk.c |    3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/editors/awk.c
+++ b/editors/awk.c
@@ -2471,6 +2471,9 @@
 						eo++;
 					if (b[eo] != '\0')
 						break;
+				} else if (p > rp && b[p-1] == '\n') {
+					/* at EOF, a last record ends at its newline */
+					so--;
 				}
 			}
 		}
